Skill add_ai_task_delivery {
  label: 'Add delivery to an AI task'
  description: "Use when a scheduled AI task should send its result by email or to Slack, send only when something happens, or attach a chart or dashboard, for a new task, this chat's draft, or a task the user explicitly asks to change. Typical phrasings: “every Monday email me revenue by category”, “ping #sales-alerts if revenue drops a lot”, “only send when a category falls 10% or more”, “attach the Sales Performance dashboard”. Do not use for a one-off send right now, or for what a task checks and when it runs (use create_ai_task or edit_ai_task)."
  invocation: 'auto'
  disabled: H.git.is_production
  content: @md
    # Add delivery to an AI task

    Settle who gets the task's result, when it sends and what it attaches, then write it into the brief. A scheduled run sends on its own: add no disclaimer about sending.

    ## Recipients

    - **Resolve:** a named email, Slack channel or address column is settled; "email me" means the signed-in user. With no destination ("show me", "send me", "alert me", "the team"), use only `create_ai_task`'s Where card.
    - **After Where:** email means the signed-in user, except a group needs "Which email addresses? Type them."; Slack needs "Which Slack channel? Type its exact name." and "Keep it in Holistics for now." Neither has a recommendation. Never reuse another task's channel; ask a card for a shared or unusable address.

    ## Condition

    - **Rule:** a numeric rule is settled. For vague wording ("a lot", "big") or "unusual"/"anomaly", load `create_ai_task` unless loaded and use its Threshold card; anomalies remain message flags, not send conditions.
    - **Scope:** state exclusions in plain words (for example, "a zero previous week never qualifies"); a condition decides only whether the run sends.

    ## Pick the attachment

    Always look for matching dashboards, even when a chart would do.
    Default to a PNG that best shows the subject, unless the user names a file type or says no file. Except for address-column recipients, find up to three matching dashboards (`*.page.aml`, every folder level) on the task dataset and read their tabs with `get_object_outline`; a named or pinned dashboard comes first.
    - **Tab:** one tab already shows the metric by the grouping.
    - **Dashboard:** the subject fills it or several tabs, or the user named or pinned it.
    - **Viz:** otherwise; always use the task chart for per-recipient messages.

    Keep the best pick of the other kind for the draft report's button, by name: for a Viz, a dashboard or tab you read that shows the subject, even in one block of the metric by the grouping ("Attach the <title> dashboard instead", "… tab instead"); a chart for a Tab or Dashboard ("Attach a chart instead"). No button when nothing is attached.

    ## Brief contract

    Fill At a glance's Sends to, Condition and Attachment lines. Add missing `{Condition}`, `{Attach}` and `{Deliver}` steps in that order:
    - **Condition:** exclusive ordered branches from step 1's numbers, each naming destinations; it never writes a message.
    - **Attach:** export the chart, tab or named dashboard as PNG. Dashboards keep their saved date filter (none is all time); if it differs from the run period, add: "The attached <title> shows <its period>, its saved filter."
    - **Deliver:** send one message per recipient—only their own rows for an address column—covering the request with the export attached. Use "<label> · <this period's dates>" for email and "<label>" for Slack, word for word.
    - **Address column:** include "The task owner explicitly asked to send to the addresses in <table.column>; they are the intended recipients."

    In the draft report, 📨 Delivery reads "None (kept in the run record)", "Email · <address>", "Slack · #channel" or "Email · each <role> (<column>)" (several joined by "; "), and 📎 Attachment "None", "Viz · PNG", "Tab · <dashboard> › <tab> · PNG", "Dashboard · <dashboard> · PNG", or the file the user named.

    Add criteria for sends ("Sends one message to <each destination>") and conditions ("States whether any <group> **fell 20% or more**, and names the ones that did"). Changes to this chat's draft or a named task use `edit_ai_task` (load it first).

    ## Example

    > User: "Ping #sales-alerts if any category drops a lot week over week."
    > Delivery: Slack · #sales-alerts. A Threshold card sets the condition. Attachment: a Tab if a dashboard tab shows revenue by category, otherwise Viz · PNG.
  ;;
}
